  third_party/clausewitz_mcp contains unchanged runtime Python source and the
  original license. UPSTREAM.json records each original path and SHA-256. Binary
  caches, generated game tables and research dumps are not included.

  hoi4_live/engine/clausewitz/memory.py is derived from calling/mem.py's typed
  read methods. It extracts portable primitives; native access is provided by
  owned Windows/macOS/Linux adapters. The original MIT notice and permission
  text are retained in hoi4_live/engine/clausewitz/LICENSE and shipped with it.

  The structured game model, ordinary-command vocabulary, bounded turn waits,
  verified-order cache and province-graph ideas inform the ongoing integration.
  native/src/{memory,game,calendar,technology,research,research_ui,technology_nodes,own_focus}.rs and native/src/platform/linux.rs port
  those typed reads, own-country focus/research semantics, process interface and
  calendar. native/PROVENANCE.md records source files; native/LICENSE.clausewitz
  retains the MIT notice. Current Linux layouts were recovered independently.
  The own economy and division observation APIs also consult Clausewitz-MCP
  semantics. Their current-build trigger, handle and location layouts and all
  renderer/input guards are independently recovered project work; observations
  do not authorize engine calls or reveal foreign-unit payload.
  native/src/production_lines/equipment.rs consults calling/game.py's
  _load_equipment and production_lines for base-equipment naming semantics.
  Fresh catalog membership, current-build layouts and own-line guards are
  independent project code; no custom design or allocation authority is implied.
  native/src/construction.rs and native/src/construction/buildings.rs consult
  calling/game.py's construction_queue and building catalog semantics. Current
  Linux types, scalar names and template joins were independently recovered;
  cost and produced work are distinct. construction/location.rs independently
  derives optional selected own-territory IDs with ownership/control and reciprocal
  catalog/status guards. construction/ui.rs independently recovers current Linux
  panel ownership, row-handle and named text bindings. construction/selection.rs
  independently derives owned manager selection with fresh public template joins;
  selection is not placement eligibility or routing authority. No foreign geography
  payload or input is authorized.
  construction/controls.rs and controls/binding.rs independently recover the
  nested topbar path, canonical choice items, exact ordinary callback captures
  and scoped local gates. Existing typed geometry is reused within one witnessed
  read; these associations execute no callback and authorize no construction input.
  production_lines/control_snapshot.rs and production_lines/controls.rs add
  independently recovered Linux production-row and ordinary factory-button
  observations, reusing the attributed own-line semantics and GNU name reader.
  These modules execute no engine callback and enable no production input.
  native/src/graph_kernel.rs independently implements bounded components and
  multi-source breadth-first search, consulting calling/doctrine.py and
  calling/ragemicro.py. It operates on caller-supplied public/generated topology;
  graph reachability establishes no military access, supply or action authority.
  The node_binding module independently observes ordinary control/callback data
  associations; it grants no input authority and executes no engine callback.

  native/src/gui/macos.rs independently recovers this build's graphics and
  SDL Cocoa geometry, runtime ObjC offsets and reciprocal window associations.
  native/src/own_focus/catalog.rs reuses the attributed own-focus semantics
  and the independently verified Mac layouts without Linux UI traversal.
  Neither path executes a game callback or writes game memory.

  native/src/construction/mac_ui.rs and construction/mac_panel.rs independently
  recover the current Mac construction view, own GUI ownership, named topbar
  opener and callback data. construction/mac_panel/routing.rs independently
  maps the own renderer, complete mouse-route arrays and cursor conversions.
  construction/mac_panel/shortcut.rs independently maps the current ordinary
  T shortcut and preceding supported keyboard receivers. The default-off
  launch/macos/construction_open.rs adapter uses ordinary macOS key events,
  typed original bindings and strict durable receipts; it executes no engine
  callback or memory write. Physical delivery remains subject to live qualification.
  They reuse the attributed construction semantics
  without copying upstream UI code or another platform's offsets. These readers
  execute no callback and grant no placement or input authority.

  The durable observation producer extends that own-state model to the separately
  verified Mac layouts with exact process/scope persistence. The Mac recording
  bridge is an independent ScreenCaptureKit integration; it has no game-input
  or engine-call path.

  Private Linux validation proved selected ordinary actions, but a running-game
  pause timed out. External engine posting remains quarantined. Source
  inclusion alone does not enable upstream commands in campaign dispatch.
